ken container the ticket exists to catch"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the 'How expected is computed' section a parallel paragraph defining `present`: present is TRUE iff the store resolves to a valid tracker (e.g. HEAD resolves), FALSE for a missing dir OR a partial clone with no resolvable HEAD — matching the described live box.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py as a consumer of the MCP /health body and state that the `in_flight` key is preserved alongside the new `store` object (updating the exact-equality assertions accordingly).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0444,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py:329 `assert idle == {\"in_flight\": 0}`; :331-332, :347, :488, :492, :495 all assert `health.json() == {\"in_flight\": 0}` (exact dict equality)","src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:120 returns `JSONResponse({\"in_flight\": gauge.value})` — the only key today","The plan's edit set names _mcp_health.py implicitly but does not list test_mcp_http_transport.py as a consumer that a body-shape change requires updating"],"finding":"The MCP `/health` response body is consumed by existing exact-dict-equality assertions in tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py; adding a `store` object to that body will turn them RED, and the plan does not enumerate them or state that the existing `in_flight` key is preserved.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdef60cb6ad62348b","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (first bullet: '/health reports the store as a structured object {path, present, expected}')","norm_id":"n3c4cce517907dfd7","priority":0.7556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Adding the {path,present,expected} store object to the MCP /health JSON body changes the top-level dict, breaking `== {\"in_flight\": 0}` assertions"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Note in the edit set that _mcp_health.py's handler adds `store` while keeping `in_flight`, and that test_mcp_http_transport.py's `== {\"in_flight\": 0}` assertions must be relaxed to check the two keys independently.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify how RemovedInputError 'fails hard' at the /health boundary (propagate vs. return a distinct error response) so it does not reintroduce a restart loop under `restart: always`.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["a health probe that can fail turns a config problem into a restart loop under restart: always","the one deliberate exception is RemovedInputError, which must still fail hard"],"finding":"AC criterion 'store_status() never raises ... the one deliberate exception is RemovedInputError, which must still fail hard' — the plan does not state what 'fail hard' means for the health probe under `restart: always`. If RemovedInputError propagates out of the handler it could crash the probe/service (the very restart-loop the other clause guards against), yet the criterion is silent on how it surfaces.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c9aa7ec60c32fb4","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC line 'store_status() never raises for an ordinary resolution fault ... the one deliberate exception is RemovedInputError'","norm_id":"n66c19294749c6fa9","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["RemovedInputError is raised on a config that references a removed input; if it propagates through /health it could put the container into a restart loop"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_stat